    <briefdescription>
<para>Additional information about basic blocks where the current variable is live. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Such a block will look like one of these templates:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>| o<mdash/>x | Internal to block. Variable is only live in this block.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>|<mdash/>x | Live-in, kill.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>| o<mdash/>| Def, live-out.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>|<mdash/>x o<mdash/>| Live-in, kill, def, live-out. Counted by NumGapBlocks.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>|<mdash/>o<mdash/>o<mdash/>| Live-through with uses or defs.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>|--------<mdash/>| Live-through without uses. Counted by NumThroughBlocks.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Two <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_split_analysis_1_1_block_info" kindref="compound">BlockInfo</ref> entries are created for template 4. One for the live-in segment, and one for the live-out segment. These entries look as if the block were split in the middle where the live range isn&apos;t live.</para>
<para>Live-through blocks without any uses don&apos;t get <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_split_analysis_1_1_block_info" kindref="compound">BlockInfo</ref> entries. They are simply listed in ThroughBlocks instead. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
